From 228f7f6827024e66c0dc28268dc326fe30cafb3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahrokh <design@cariblanco.best>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 04:41:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] layer split: measure --batch-mtp's acceptance (the
 batch path never reported it)

The admitted request printed DONE ... 0 of 0 (it decoded one token) and the per-window decisions lived in batch_step, unreported.  A pure DraftAccept accumulator (stage_plan.hpp, host-tested) now counts one proposal per active slot per window: the target picked it when the window's two rows of that slot agree.  Each slot's BDONE ends with accepted, offered (appended, so an older reader is unaffected); the strata batch: summary reports the period's rate, absent without the flag.
